                "quote": "match c.DueBack with | Some due -> $\"on loan until {due}\" | None -> \"on shelf\""
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The change adds no new domain rule. Branch existence comes from Tier 2 (Catalog.findBranch, which yields the 'unknown branch' error). Copies at a branch come from Catalog.copiesAt. Holds queues reuse the existing holdQueue projection, and member type text reuses memberTypeName/ofMember. Tier 3 only sorts by id and formats CSV rows from view models. The on loan / on shelf status is a projection of the existing DueBack field, not a new rule. The CLI only parses words and renders views.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 9,
                "quote": "-open System.IO"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 18,
                "quote": "ports.Files.WriteLines path (\"copy,member,due,days overdue\" :: rows)"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Reports.fs",
                "line": 35,
                "quote": "ports.Files.WriteLines path (\"copy,book,title,status\" :: rows)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "All new file writes go through the existing Files port, and state is read through ports.Store.Load(). The change also fixes an existing Tier 3 System.IO violation: exportOverdue now uses ports.Files instead of File.WriteAllLines, with the same behaviour. Tier 1/2 has no effects, and the CLI does not re-enter Tier 2 or persistence. For an unknown branch, the write happens inside Result.map after the branch lookup, so nothing is written.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 101,
                "quote": "Book = BookId.value copy.Book"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 116,
                "quote": "|> List.map ofMember"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "Each fact the change uses has one definition, referenced everywhere: due date from the loan, queue order and since date from holdQueue, member type name from ofMember/memberTypeName, the branch's copies from Catalog.copiesAt. No limit, date rule or status derivation is copied as a literal into another tier.",
